  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "4169bf2b-cff9-4c51-801f-17ab0f159714",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1856,
        688
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 832,
        "content": "## Upsert and merchandise Medusa products from a PIM\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow receives a product launch payload from a PIM, validates it, and looks up the product in Medusa by handle. It updates an existing product or creates a new priced product, normalizes the branch output, then merchandises the product by assigning it to a category, collection, and sales channel. Finally, it builds and returns a launch response to the webhook caller.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the webhook URL in the PIM so product launch events are sent to the \"Receive product launch\" trigger.\n- Set up Medusa credentials in n8n for all Medusa nodes, including the correct backend URL and API token.\n- Confirm the payload fields expected by the validation code, especially handle, pricing, category_id, collection_id, and sales channel identifiers.\n- Verify the Medusa category, collection, and sales channel IDs referenced by the payload or node parameters exist in the target store.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the validation code and Set nodes to match your PIM schema, and modify the Medusa merchandising steps if products should be assigned to different categories, collections, or sales channels."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
